# Windows batch files MUST check out with CRLF. cmd.exe mishandles LF-only
# .bat files — a fresh clone on a machine with core.autocrlf=false would get an
# installer that fails with "'install.bat' is not recognized" (found the hard
# way in slice 37, by actually running it rather than trusting it).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Everything else: normalise in the repo, let git decide on checkout.
* text=auto
